00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:36.710
Now let's take a look at how
we build an app with App Maker.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:39.035
I'll show how we do this
in five easy stages.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.500
The first one is to
define your data model

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.850
and connect to data sources.

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:49.090
This means that we have to
define what data our app

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.250
is going to be working with.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.020
And the most popular
way to do this

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:57.130
is to import a table
from a spreadsheet, which

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:58.840
can be done easily.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.690
And that creates a table
in the SQL database

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:04.210
that is created
automatically for every app

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:07.190
that we start building.

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:09.080
If you don't have a
sheet with a table ready,

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:12.200
you can define your
data model manually

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.900
by defining the
fields, one by one.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:22.700
The second stage is to design
the UI of the web application.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:27.560
Here, anyone can choose from a
palette of widgets what the web

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:32.890
pages will look like, for
both data entry using forms

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:37.630
and to present data to the users
of the application in tables

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:38.990
and other widgets, like maps.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:45.240
You can also change
the styling here

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.180
by formatting the
spaces on the page

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.580
and what the overall
layout will look.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:55.540
And you can also adjust it to
be good for mobile devices.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.270
You can also apply
your brand identity,

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.990
as we saw for our customers,
with HTML and CSS code that

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:02.100
will run on the browser.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:12.010
The next phase is to bind
the data to the UI elements

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:14.500
and trigger in-app events.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.380
This is the stage where
you actually outline

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.820
the flow of the application.

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:21.130
You decide what
happens once somebody

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:25.210
enters data, for
example, and also

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.540
invoke automatic actions,
like sending an email,

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:31.900
or just stitching the
flow of the internal logic

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:36.590
of the workflow that
you're automating.

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:42.450
Once this stage is done, we move
over to defining the user role.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:46.010
As I mentioned earlier, users
of the app can be different

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:48.740
and can have different
permissions to do

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.060
different actions in the app.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.900
Some people enter
data into the app,

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:55.580
some people view reports, some
other people take actions.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:15:00.240
So we can define all these
roles inside the app.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:02.630
And once this phase
is done, we can

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:06.170
preview our app to see what
it will look like in reality.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:10.850
And once it looks fine to us, we
can publish it into the domain

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:12.710
and then other users
can start using it.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:22.510
To start building App
Maker apps in your company,

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:25.240
please check out
Google's Developer site

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:26.470
on the App Maker section.

