Right now, this is not possible.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:21.580
The reason is that we follow
strict security policies

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.070
with Google Cloud and G Suite.

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:26.200
The way that we are
going to approach this

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.050
is to extend the
reach of App Maker

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:33.870
both to users and domains
in several stages.

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:37.210
And one of the first ones
would be to share applications

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:38.830
across domain.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.720
The way to do that
right now is, let's

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.280
say, between two
different companies,

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:45.880
you can package your
application in the first domain

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:49.240
and send it over to the
second domain offline,

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:53.450
and then deploy that
application in that domain.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:56.330
One of the other areas that
we are looking to expand

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:59.150
is to allow users outside
of the G Suite domain

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:01.160
to use the App Maker
apps, but we still

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.930
don't have an ETA
for this feature.

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:05.960
So stay tuned in the
following quarters

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:07.040
to hear when we do that.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:13.360
Next question, can you
build mobile applications

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.710
with App Maker?

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.180
So, the answer is yes.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.490
And we have various
customers that have already

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:20.770
deployed mobile applications.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:26.110
The way they did it is that they
designed the web pages to fit

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:29.410
mobile screens and tested them.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:31.870
And they are already
using them in production.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:37.270
We do not have ways to support
complete responsive design

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:38.702
in App Maker right now.

00:19:38.702 --> 00:19:40.910
But what we are going to do
in the following quarters

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:43.000
is to provide
interim stages where

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.630
you can have
different viewports,

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:49.840
and also design the
breakpoints in your screens

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:55.000
so that applications look
better on mobile devices.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.360
In the future, we'll also
have mobile-specific widgets.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:04.460
But these will probably
come sometime in 2019.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:07.220
Next question,
besides Cloud SQL,

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:09.990
can you connect to
other databases?

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:12.090
As I mentioned during
the presentation,

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:16.230
we support any database
that can be accessed

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:19.080
through JDBC or a REST API.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:22.260
That covers a lot of
databases in the market.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:26.520
And you can connect to
those databases by coding,

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:31.470
as part of the app, a service
that will access that API.

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:34.710
So you can add access
to any database

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:38.250
that you have, either already
working in your company

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.950
or that you want to deploy
with an App Maker app.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.020
It will involve coding, though.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:47.770
So if you don't want to have any
coding involved with accessing

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:50.880
a database, we recommend
using the default

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:56.070
Cloud SQL that can
accommodate any data imported

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:57.585
from various sources.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:06.480
Is it possible to build
workflow apps with App Maker?

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:07.380
Yes.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:12.450
I think we try to like
demo here an application

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:15.060
built by Globe Telecom,
for example, that

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:17.580
showed how a travel
approval process, which

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:23.130
is a workflow starting from an
employee asking for a travel

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:25.740
itinerary to be
approved, mentioning

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:28.440
the reasons for the travel,
the business need for that.

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:31.710
That goes on to a
second person that

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:38.040
calculates the cost of the
travel suggested, and also sees

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.830
whether it's in
cap or out of cap

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:44.040
or requires specific approval
from the financial point

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:44.890
of view.

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:47.010
Once this is approved,
a manager has

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:49.770
to approve this,
and finally, someone

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:56.940
from the operations that does
all the travel, like bookings.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:59.800
So all this process has been
built in a single App Maker

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:00.300
app.

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:02.008
There are different
types of users there.

00:22:02.008 --> 00:22:05.130
There are people that file their
approval requests and people

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:07.680
that review it and approve it.

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:09.864
And that's an
example of a workflow

00:22:09.864 --> 00:22:11.280
that you can build
with App Maker.

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:12.480
There are many more.

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:16.290
And you can also check
out some of our templates

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:18.784
inside the product to see
other workflows that can

00:22:18.784 --> 00:22:19.950
be supported by the product.

00:22:23.430 --> 00:22:26.970
To summarize, I'd like to remind
that App Maker is a new G Suite

00:22:26.970 --> 00:22:31.620
product that allows to build web
applications with easy access

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:36.600
to G Suite APIs and
a built-in Cloud SQL

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:38.610
database, over
which you can build

00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:41.520
line-of-business
applications and workflow

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:44.520
operations in your
company pretty easily.

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:47.360
And to check those out and
try them themselves, please

00:22:47.360 --> 00:22:52.480
refer to our Developers site
under App Makers section.

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:53.960
Thank you so much for watching.

00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:56.230
Please tune in next Tuesday
for the next Cloud OnAir.

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:02.580
[MUSIC PLAYING]

